WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.680
Service standards, honest selling and your customer list.

2
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:08.380
This is the video for module 3 of Customer Relations and Sales.

3
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:18.760
Without written standards, service depends on mood: excellent when you are rested, poor when you are tired. Customers notice the bad days most.

4
00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:25.130
Honest selling is not weak selling. Customers who trust you return and recommend you.

5
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.140
And a simple customer list shows who buys, how often, and who has gone quiet.

6
00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:43.480
A service standard is a clear promise about how you treat customers, written down so you and any helper can keep it. Reply quickly is not a standard, because you cannot check it.

7
00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:52.130
Reply to every message within 1 hour, 8am to 7pm, is a standard. You can check whether you did it.

8
00:00:52.480 --> 00:01:00.360
Choose promises you can keep on your busiest day, not your best day. A smaller promise kept is better than a big promise broken.

9
00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:14.960
Nigeria's consumer protection law expects accurate information and honest claims. First, never say a cream, tea or soap cures a disease. That is a medical claim, and NAFDAC rules are strict.

10
00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:20.780
Do not call a product original or imported unless you are sure it is true.

11
00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:27.490
Do not invent scarcity. Only 2 left, or price goes up tonight, when it is not true.

12
00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.870
Use real photos of real stock.

13
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:37.390
Never write fake reviews, and never add delivery or packaging fees after payment.

14
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:44.700
Before you post any sales message, ask four questions. Is it true? Can you prove every claim?

15
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:49.470
Is it fair? Would you be happy if a seller treated your mother this way?

16
00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.220
Would you say it in public, in front of your whole church or market association?

17
00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.760
Will she still be happy next month, after using the product?

18
00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:16.050
Comfort in Benin City first wrote: miracle cream, cures eczema. She had no proof. She rewrote it: rich shea and cocoa butter cream for dry skin, patch test first if you have sensitive skin. Honest, and still attractive.

19
00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:25.740
Your memory is not a reliable customer list. Choose a notebook, a free Google Sheet, or WhatsApp Business labels plus a notebook.

20
00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:31.090
Start with name, phone number with permission, date, items and amount.

21
00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:41.130
Then add notes, like whether she prefers unscented, and a next follow-up date. Reading the note before you reply makes her feel remembered.

22
00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:45.730
Record every sale daily, and review the list once a month.

23
00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:52.670
Lock your phone, never share the list, and only message people who agreed to receive your offers.

24
00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.380
Here is how the list guides you. Ada keeps a Google Sheet.

25
00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:03.320
In March she recorded 30 orders worth 285,000 naira.

26
00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:11.930
Her average order is 285,000 divided by 30, which is 9,500 naira.

27
00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:24.250
Of 22 customers, 14 had bought before. And she finds 6 regulars who have not bought in over 8 weeks. She sends each a personal check-in, and two of them reorder within the week.

28
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:37.000
To remember. A standard is a specific promise you can check, so review it every week. Never make cure claims, fake scarcity or fake reviews. Use the four-question test.

29
00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:42.600
And each month, count your repeat customers, your average order and your quiet customers.

30
00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:58.480
Your turn. Write five service standards and keep a tally for one week. Check five of your recent posts and rewrite any that fail the test. Start your customer list with at least 10 customers, and mark three for a follow-up this week.

31
00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.770
Continue with the lessons below.
